# Worldbook root. The legacy v1 CONTENT stays out of git: the eight old content directories
# (rules / personality_background / unnamed_persona / voice_mapping / event_data / debt /
# dialogue_history / compressed_memory) are dead -- the runtime rejects awake.worldbook.v1
# (WB2-SCHEMA-UNSUPPORTED:entry) and no code under src/ reads them.
# Two things under here DO ship, because the runtime reads them straight from the module:
#   * persona_definitions/ -- build-time EmbeddedResource for Persona Workbench
#     (PersonaWorkbench.Core.csproj) plus the source manifest and handoff validators.
#     It is tag vocabulary, not world book content.
#   * manifest.json + packages/ -- the repository-side package form (2026-09-14, see
#     docs/worldbook-studio-plan/RUNTIME-MAPPING-CONTRACT.md). manifest.json is the registry
#     (awake.worldbook.registry.v1); packages/<world>/ holds the compiled runtime three
#     (manifest.json + runtime.json + index.json). src/WorldbookRuntime.cs walks up from the
#     assembly directory and accepts ONLY registry.v1 / awake.worldbook.v2, so without these
#     files the module ships no world book at all.
AWAKE/ModuleData/Worldbook/*
!AWAKE/ModuleData/Worldbook/persona_definitions/
!AWAKE/ModuleData/Worldbook/manifest.json
!AWAKE/ModuleData/Worldbook/packages/

# Embedded framework: download caches and generated storage fixtures
